@ cases.runtime-integer-explains-unchecked-dependent-call
files_tote = "app"
files."app/Tauto.eure" = 'package { name = "app"
version = "0.1.0" }'
extract = true
files."app/src/main.taut" = ```tauto
import std::Nat
inductive Box: (Nat) -> Type { Mk(n: Nat): Box(n) }
fn read(n: Nat, value: Box(n)): Nat { n }
fn demo(): i64 { read(0, Mk(0)) }
```
load_error = "`demo` is not checked by the kernel: it uses `i64`, which runs as written: `i64` is a runtime integer type; for checked code, import `std::SInt` and use `I64`, constructed with a proof that the value is in range; it extracts to `i64`"

